A linear probe on LaBraM reads braindecode's default readout, `fc_norm` applied to the mean of the patch tokens as in the authors' fine-tuning, instead of the [CLS] token, which neither pretraining nor the authors' fine-tuning read; its frozen embeddings no longer pass the patch tokens through the pretrained final norm, so extract them again. CBraMod needs no change: braindecode 2.1 no longer runs `proj_out`, the head that reconstructs masked patches in pretraining.
